&lt;p&gt;Short answer: for a logistics receipt system, use a backend-authorized direct browser upload with short-lived signed URLs, immutable object keys, and a storage policy that treats tenant isolation as the first constraint. React and Next.js can send the bytes directly to S3-compatible storage; the application server should decide who may create, read, replace, or delete a receipt. CORS is part of that boundary, not a substitute for authorization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The easiest architecture is the one that leaves the fewest dangerous decisions in the browser. A browser upload should carry a file and a temporary capability. It should not carry a cloud master key, choose an unrestricted object path, or decide that a receipt belongs to tenant A because a form field said so.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That sounds strict because audit storage is strict. A receipt is evidence, not merely an image attached to a record.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No magic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Receipt authorization starts with a failure test
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Usually, yes, when the files are large enough that routing every byte through a Next.js server adds cost and failure surface. The server authenticates the user, resolves the tenant from the session, validates the proposed receipt metadata, creates an object key, and returns a short-lived signed upload URL. The browser then uploads directly to the object store. A later download uses the same shape: authorize on the server, mint a temporary read URL, and let the browser fetch the private object.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The URL is a capability with a narrow scope. Its useful properties are an operation, an object, and an expiry. The browser must not receive the storage account credential that can create arbitrary objects or enumerate another tenant's prefix. A signed URL also doesn't make the object public; it grants the holder temporary access to the operation it represents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CORS answers a different question. It asks whether a browser origin may make the cross-origin request. It does not establish that the logged-in person owns the receipt. Configure the exact production origin and the preview-origin policy you actually intend to support, then test the upload from a real browser. A command-line request can prove that the endpoint accepts bytes; it cannot prove that the browser's origin checks are correct.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For private files, keep the database as the authority for ownership and lifecycle state. The object store holds bytes. The database says which tenant owns the receipt, which upload is accepted, which review state applies, and when a retention rule permits deletion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How should React and Next.js handle signed URLs when a duplicate receipt becomes a reliability failure?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A private bucket is a useful baseline, not a complete isolation design. The critical question is where tenant identity enters the object key and where it is checked again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use a server-derived key with a tenant identifier and an opaque receipt identifier, for example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataclasses&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataclass&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;uuid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@dataclass&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;frozen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ReceiptUpload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;tenant_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;upload_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;extension&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;object_key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;upload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ReceiptUpload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;extension&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;upload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;extension&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lower&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lstrip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;allowed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"pdf"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"jpg"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"jpeg"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"png"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;extension&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;allowed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ValueError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"unsupported receipt type"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"tenants/{upload.tenant_id}/receipts/"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"{upload.receipt_id}/uploads/{upload.upload_id}/original.{extension}"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The tenant ID in this example is not permission by itself. It is a namespace that makes mistakes easier to detect and listing by prefix more useful. The authorization check must compare the authenticated principal with the tenant record before generating the key. On download, perform that comparison again before issuing a signed URL. Trusting a key supplied by the client is the classic path from a harmless upload form to an object-level authorization bug.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I treat a &lt;code&gt;409&lt;/code&gt; during receipt finalization as a state conflict, not as permission to overwrite whichever object happens to be at the requested filename. The application can keep an upload in &lt;code&gt;received&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;validated&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;accepted&lt;/code&gt; state and make the transition idempotent. If two tabs submit the same receipt, a unique database constraint on the upload identity should arbitrate the race.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is why immutable keys matter. Reusing &lt;code&gt;tenant-17/receipts/May.pdf&lt;/code&gt; makes a replacement look like an ordinary successful write, while a unique upload ID preserves the original object until the application explicitly applies its retention policy. Object stores are good at storing objects; they are not a substitute for the business transaction that decides which object is authoritative.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How should a team choose direct browser upload with presigned storage access?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Compare responsibilities, not the number of lines in the first demo. A managed storage integration may feel easiest because it sits beside an existing database and authentication system. Direct S3-compatible storage may feel easiest because the team controls origin rules and signed-request details. A hosted edge store may simplify geographic delivery while introducing its own configuration model. None of those labels answers the tenant-isolation question for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Path&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it makes convenient&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Trade-off to verify&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Application-managed storage integration&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Keeping authentication, metadata, and file operations in one application boundary&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Confirm that its authorization model maps cleanly to tenant ownership and private signed access&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S3 presigned upload&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Letting the backend mint a narrowly scoped upload while the browser transfers bytes directly&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The team owns bucket policy, CORS, retention, recovery tests, and the operational burden around them&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;R2 direct browser upload&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sending browser traffic to an object store rather than through the application server&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Validate private download behavior, allowed origins, and the regional or jurisdictional fit before rollout&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Self-hosted S3-compatible service&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Keeping deployment and data placement under the team's control&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The team also owns durability, upgrades, monitoring, backups, and incident recovery&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The comparison changes when the application already has a strong data boundary. A Supabase-based team may reasonably value keeping storage policy near its existing auth and database policy. A team already operating S3 may prefer its established IAM, lifecycle, and audit process. R2 can be reasonable when its direct-upload and delivery model matches the product. Those are integration decisions, not universal rankings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The catch is operational ownership. A path is not suitable when the frontend team needs to add preview origins but has no safe process for changing CORS, or when compliance requires a location and replication design the chosen service cannot provide. Stick with the option whose failure and recovery controls your team can actually operate. A shorter setup guide is not evidence of stronger isolation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  European governance for CORS and retention
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start the European review with the data, not with a region dropdown. Receipts can contain addresses, names, tax details, and images of paperwork. The organization needs to decide the applicable residency, processor, retention, deletion, and access-review requirements; I'm not sure which legal interpretation applies to a particular logistics business without that context. The technical design should record the chosen location and policy, but it cannot make that legal decision.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Geography also affects the recovery plan. Ask where the primary objects live, where backups live, how a tenant deletion propagates, and how the team proves that an expired receipt is no longer retrievable. Amazon's object lifecycle documentation is a useful reminder that retention automation is a storage policy, while Google Cloud's storage documentation shows the breadth of controls that must be evaluated in a cloud storage design. The exact feature set still needs verification for the selected service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CORS deserves a concrete test matrix. Include the production origin, every permitted preview origin pattern, an unapproved origin, a signed upload, a signed download, and a failed preflight. Check the allowed methods and headers used by the actual browser client. Do not solve a CORS failure by making the bucket public; that trades a configuration problem for an access-control failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lifecycle rules should match the business clock. A day-scale deletion rule is not the same thing as a ten-minute download URL, and neither one is a legal hold. Keep retention state in the application, apply storage lifecycle rules as a backstop, and define what happens to abandoned multipart uploads or partially completed transfers. The policy must be observable: an operator should be able to answer why an object still exists without searching browser logs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Rollout: can the authorization path survive retries?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Roll out the authorization path before optimizing transfer speed. A small backend service can make the decisions explicit:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;datetime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;datetime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;timedelta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;timezone&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;authorize_receipt_upload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;datetime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;timezone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;utc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PermissionError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"authentication required"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tenant_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tenant_ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PermissionError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"tenant access denied"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"awaiting_upload"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"retryable"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ValueError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"receipt is not accepting an upload"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="n"&gt;expires_at&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;timedelta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;minutes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"tenant_id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tenant_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"receipt_id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"object_key"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;object_key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;receipt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;upload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expires_at"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;expires_at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isoformat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"operation"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"upload"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The grant expires in 10 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The actual signer is deliberately behind this decision function. Whether the implementation calls an S3-compatible SDK, a REST endpoint, or an existing storage integration, it must not bypass the tenant check. Store the generated upload identity and expected object key before handing the URL to React. After the browser reports completion, verify the object metadata and mark the database row as received; only a later validation step should make it accepted for audit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider a dispatcher working from a depot with an unstable connection. The browser obtains a URL, uploads most of a receipt, loses the connection, and retries while a second tab submits the same document. If both attempts write &lt;code&gt;receipts/current.pdf&lt;/code&gt;, a successful HTTP response tells you almost nothing about which bytes the audit record now points to. With an upload ID in the key, a database uniqueness rule, and a finalization transition, the two objects remain distinguishable; one can be rejected as a duplicate without erasing the other. That extra identity is more valuable than a clever upload component because it gives operations a record to inspect after the browser has disappeared.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test in stages. First, unit-test key construction and authorization with cross-tenant cases. Next, run browser tests against a non-production bucket using the same CORS shape as production. Then exercise expiry, retry, duplicate submission, deletion, and a user who belongs to one tenant but requests another tenant's receipt. Include a network interruption during a large upload. It is an ordinary failure, and ordinary failures deserve a designed response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Watch the signals that expose isolation mistakes: signed-URL issuance by tenant, rejected cross-tenant requests, object keys outside the expected prefix, orphaned uploads, expired objects still referenced by the database, and CORS failures by origin. Avoid logging full signed URLs because query parameters can contain the capability itself. Log a request ID and a redacted object identity instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The final decision rule is compact: choose the transfer path that keeps bytes off the application server, but choose the authorization and recovery model that keeps tenant ownership in the application database. If a service cannot meet the required region, retention, CORS ownership, or recovery behavior, it is not the easiest choice for this workload, regardless of how quickly the first upload demo works.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  References
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hola, amiguitos. Aprovechando mi tiempo de ciudadano desempleado, decidí, como buen programador, avanzar mi &lt;em&gt;side project&lt;/em&gt;. Como necesitaba un servicio de autenticación, elegí &lt;strong&gt;Entra External ID&lt;/strong&gt;, y se me ocurrió la genial idea de crear una demo que me sirviera de guía para mis futuros proyectos. ¿Por qué no? Suena bien, ¿verdad? Después de un par de semanas terminé la demo, y se me ocurrió otra "genial idea". ¿Y si documento la demo para mi &lt;em&gt;yo&lt;/em&gt; del futuro? Claro, ¿por qué no? Otros cuantos días de mi vida perdidos. Cuando al fin terminé, ansioso por continuar mi proyecto, se me volvió a ocurrir otra brillante idea. ¿Y si comparto esta documentación? ¡Claro!, ¿por qué no? Tal vez con esto podría conseguir trabajo (spoiler… no pasará). Y después de varios días mejorando mi pequeña doc, henos aquí... Espero que les sirva, hijos de p#t@.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nota:&lt;/strong&gt; Los textos de esta guía fueron redactados y revisados con ayuda de la IA. ¿Ustedes creen que yo sé de reglas gramaticales? Y claro que también me ayudó a buscar documentación actualizada de Azure. ¿Quién todavía busca manualmente en Google? En fin, para seguir esta guía deben conocer los conceptos básicos de programación (JWT, scope, claim, etc.) y de Azure (Entra ID, suscripción, etc.).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En esta guía configuraremos paso a paso &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Entra External ID&lt;/strong&gt;, el servicio de Microsoft para que los usuarios de una aplicación puedan registrarse e iniciar sesión.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Como ejemplo usaremos &lt;strong&gt;Blurlink&lt;/strong&gt;, un proyecto ficticio. Vamos a crear un tenant de tipo External, registrar el backend y el frontend en &lt;strong&gt;App registrations&lt;/strong&gt; y configurar un &lt;em&gt;user flow&lt;/em&gt; de registro e inicio de sesión.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Al final conectaremos un frontend en React y una API en NestJS, solo para ver el flujo completo funcionando. &lt;strong&gt;Nada de lo que configuraremos en Entra depende del lenguaje ni del framework, así que también sirve para proyectos con otras tecnologías.&lt;/strong&gt; Entonces empecemos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fy8atdlul1odymyledze7.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fy8atdlul1odymyledze7.png" alt="Tipos de tenant" width="769" height="373"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Los tenants pueden ser de tipo &lt;strong&gt;Workforce&lt;/strong&gt; (para empleados) o &lt;strong&gt;External&lt;/strong&gt; (para clientes). Las cuentas de Azure traen por defecto un tenant de tipo Workforce llamado "Default Directory". Por eso empezaremos creando un nuevo tenant de tipo &lt;strong&gt;External&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nota:&lt;/strong&gt; Al tenant también se le llama &lt;em&gt;directory&lt;/em&gt;, por eso en el portal veremos nombres como Default Directory o Directories + subscriptions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Crear el tenant externo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En el portal de Azure buscamos &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Entra ID&lt;/strong&gt; y en &lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt; le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Manage tenants&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 01]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fb98hbhvcvtthc033dda3.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fb98hbhvcvtthc033dda3.png" alt="Imagen 01" width="800" height="394"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 01



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Manage tenants&lt;/strong&gt;, creamos un nuevo tenant con &lt;strong&gt;Create&lt;/strong&gt; (por ahora solo existe el Default Directory de tipo &lt;strong&gt;Workforce&lt;/strong&gt;). [Imagen 02]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Foo0v20dl17eyge73u66p.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Foo0v20dl17eyge73u66p.png" alt="Imagen 02" width="799" height="274"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 02



&lt;p&gt;Elegimos la configuración &lt;strong&gt;External&lt;/strong&gt;, la que se usa para autenticar clientes, y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Continue&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 03]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fzx0tn0mqhx1gz5hnwjtj.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fzx0tn0mqhx1gz5hnwjtj.png" alt="Imagen 03" width="800" height="493"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 03



&lt;p&gt;Le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Use Azure subscription&lt;/strong&gt; para vincular el tenant a una suscripción de Azure. [Imagen 04]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk3wda5oxec209qbrgpra.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk3wda5oxec209qbrgpra.png" alt="Imagen 04" width="800" height="452"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 04



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Basics&lt;/strong&gt;, colocamos el nombre del tenant, el dominio &lt;code&gt;blurlinkdemo.onmicrosoft.com&lt;/code&gt; y la región (ni el dominio ni la región se pueden cambiar después), y continuamos con &lt;strong&gt;Next: Add a subscription&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 05]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fua6w6lu361rz0arln3a4.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fua6w6lu361rz0arln3a4.png" alt="Imagen 05" width="800" height="380"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 05



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Add a subscription&lt;/strong&gt;, elegimos la suscripción y con &lt;strong&gt;Create new&lt;/strong&gt; creamos un &lt;em&gt;resource group&lt;/em&gt; nuevo (&lt;code&gt;rg-blurlink-entraid-demo&lt;/code&gt;) en East US. Continuamos con &lt;strong&gt;Next: Review + create&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 06]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F3x4ghp08woe7utjemi0t.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F3x4ghp08woe7utjemi0t.png" alt="Imagen 06" width="800" height="393"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 06



&lt;p&gt;Revisamos el resumen y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Create&lt;/strong&gt;. La creación puede tardar hasta 30 minutos. [Imagen 07]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F99xunx0vygud71ody9x7.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F99xunx0vygud71ody9x7.png" alt="Imagen 07" width="799" height="568"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 07



&lt;p&gt;Cuando termina, Blurlink Demo aparece en &lt;strong&gt;Manage tenants&lt;/strong&gt; con tipo External. Al hacer clic en su nombre se abre &lt;strong&gt;Tenant details&lt;/strong&gt;, donde vemos su Tenant ID. Lo anotamos junto con el subdominio (&lt;code&gt;blurlinkdemo&lt;/code&gt;, lo que va antes de &lt;code&gt;.onmicrosoft.com&lt;/code&gt;), porque los vamos a usar en el frontend y en el backend. [Imagen 08]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk94i0zxfjs267gion21c.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk94i0zxfjs267gion21c.png" alt="Imagen 08" width="800" height="438"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 08



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nota:&lt;/strong&gt; External ID se cobra en la suscripción vinculada al tenant, según cuántos usuarios inician sesión cada mes. Los primeros 50.000 usuarios del mes son gratis, así que una demo como esta no tiene costo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Cambiar al tenant nuevo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A partir de aquí trabajaremos en el &lt;a href="https://entra.microsoft.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Entra admin center&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, que es el portal que usa la documentación de External ID. Todavía estamos en &lt;em&gt;Default Directory&lt;/em&gt;, así que abrimos la configuración con el ícono del engranaje de arriba a la derecha. [Imagen 09]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fss2xu4aacjegdfkepm72.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fss2xu4aacjegdfkepm72.png" alt="Imagen 09" width="800" height="545"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 09



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Directories + subscriptions&lt;/strong&gt;, buscamos el nuevo tenant &lt;strong&gt;Blurlink Demo&lt;/strong&gt; en la pestaña &lt;strong&gt;All Directories&lt;/strong&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Switch&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 10]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flm6xkha3oovlhmmtt5gk.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flm6xkha3oovlhmmtt5gk.png" alt="Imagen 10" width="800" height="472"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 10



&lt;p&gt;Ya estamos en nuestro nuevo tenant, &lt;em&gt;Blurlink Demo&lt;/em&gt;. Su nombre debe aparecer arriba a la derecha, debajo de nuestro correo, y en la página de inicio. [Imagen 11]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ftveco8ufirw64u1da1bf.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ftveco8ufirw64u1da1bf.png" alt="Imagen 11" width="800" height="536"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 11



&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Registrar la API (backend)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En el menú de la izquierda, dentro de &lt;strong&gt;Entra ID&lt;/strong&gt;, entramos a &lt;strong&gt;App registrations&lt;/strong&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;New registration&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 12]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhm4qj612ojx1titfruft.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhm4qj612ojx1titfruft.png" alt="Imagen 12" width="800" height="374"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 12



&lt;p&gt;Le ponemos de nombre &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-api&lt;/code&gt; y elegimos Single tenant only. El Redirect URI lo dejamos vacío, porque la API no inicia sesión, solo valida los tokens que le llegan. Le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Register&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 13]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fzdns28zmukhit2i1o9ia.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fzdns28zmukhit2i1o9ia.png" alt="Imagen 13" width="800" height="444"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 13



&lt;p&gt;Copiamos el &lt;strong&gt;Application (client) ID&lt;/strong&gt;. El backend lo usa para comprobar que el token es para esta API, y el frontend, para pedir ese token. Luego entramos a &lt;strong&gt;Expose an API&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 14]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0w3v2o81rcthnrdf9c01.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0w3v2o81rcthnrdf9c01.png" alt="Imagen 14" width="800" height="442"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 14



&lt;p&gt;Junto a Application ID URI le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add&lt;/strong&gt;. En el panel, el campo ya viene con el formato &lt;code&gt;api://&amp;lt;clientId&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, usando el client ID de la API. Si viene vacío o con otro valor, lo escribimos con ese formato. Guardamos con &lt;strong&gt;Save&lt;/strong&gt;. Ese valor es el prefijo de los permisos (&lt;strong&gt;scopes&lt;/strong&gt;) de la API. [Imagen 15]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhfpvfufnpapcubwhn6iu.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhfpvfufnpapcubwhn6iu.png" alt="Imagen 15" width="800" height="359"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 15



&lt;p&gt;Con &lt;strong&gt;Add a scope&lt;/strong&gt; creamos el permiso &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.Read&lt;/code&gt;. En &lt;em&gt;Who can consent&lt;/em&gt; elegimos Admins only, llenamos el nombre y la descripción que verá el administrador, dejamos State en Enabled y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add scope&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 16]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F89997ubw8set91hqrsbx.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F89997ubw8set91hqrsbx.png" alt="Imagen 16" width="800" height="452"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 16



&lt;p&gt;Repetimos lo mismo para &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.ReadWrite&lt;/code&gt; (leer y crear). Ya tenemos los dos scopes. [Imagen 17]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fz4ru5tlt6yb1slix99wd.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fz4ru5tlt6yb1slix99wd.png" alt="Imagen 17" width="800" height="427"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 17



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nota:&lt;/strong&gt; Entra arma cada access token con la configuración de la API a la que va dirigido. Por eso los claims del access token los configuraremos acá, en &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-api&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Token configuration&lt;/strong&gt; le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add optional claim&lt;/strong&gt;, elegimos el tipo &lt;em&gt;Access&lt;/em&gt;, marcamos &lt;code&gt;idtyp&lt;/code&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add&lt;/strong&gt;. Este claim indica si el token es de un usuario o solo de una aplicación. [Imagen 18]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgeqvb2is899lhf0spyug.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgeqvb2is899lhf0spyug.png" alt="Imagen 18" width="799" height="395"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 18



&lt;p&gt;Volvemos a &lt;strong&gt;Add optional claim&lt;/strong&gt; con el tipo &lt;em&gt;Access&lt;/em&gt; y marcamos &lt;code&gt;email&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;family_name&lt;/code&gt; y &lt;code&gt;given_name&lt;/code&gt; (también se pueden marcar junto con &lt;code&gt;idtyp&lt;/code&gt; en el paso anterior). El access token no trae estos datos por defecto, y los necesitamos para el mensaje de bienvenida. Le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 19]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fdqqjtp98fpyh1l028o30.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fdqqjtp98fpyh1l028o30.png" alt="Imagen 19" width="799" height="422"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 19



&lt;p&gt;Estos claims necesitan los permisos &lt;code&gt;email&lt;/code&gt; y &lt;code&gt;profile&lt;/code&gt; de &lt;em&gt;Microsoft Graph&lt;/em&gt;, por lo que puede aparecer un aviso. Marcamos la casilla para que los agregue y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 20]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fv9d0ogsp085ciqpnn8t4.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fv9d0ogsp085ciqpnn8t4.png" alt="Imagen 20" width="800" height="229"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 20



&lt;p&gt;Quedan los cuatro claims configurados en el access token. [Imagen 21]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F99f72zof9cf5bv084sz4.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F99f72zof9cf5bv084sz4.png" alt="Imagen 21" width="800" height="396"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 21



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Manifest&lt;/strong&gt; verificamos que &lt;code&gt;requestedAccessTokenVersion&lt;/code&gt; sea 2, porque el backend espera tokens v2. Si tuviera otro valor, lo cambiamos a 2 y guardamos. [Imagen 22]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ft5gk4iif3y1ap08ybjnj.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ft5gk4iif3y1ap08ybjnj.png" alt="Imagen 22" width="799" height="435"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 22



&lt;h2&gt;


  4. Registrar el frontend (SPA)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Volvemos a &lt;strong&gt;App registrations&lt;/strong&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;New registration&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 23]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fu1rys9mtc4fcg6jeghk4.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fu1rys9mtc4fcg6jeghk4.png" alt="Imagen 23" width="800" height="414"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 23



&lt;p&gt;Le ponemos de nombre &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-spa&lt;/code&gt; y elegimos Single tenant only. En Redirect URI elegimos la plataforma Single-page application (SPA) y escribimos &lt;code&gt;http://localhost:5173/redirect&lt;/code&gt;, con el puerto de Vite y la ruta exacta. Es la página del frontend a la que Entra nos devuelve al iniciar y al cerrar sesión. Le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Register&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 24]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fara1twlk4l0q8iv5joz4.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fara1twlk4l0q8iv5joz4.png" alt="Imagen 24" width="800" height="538"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 24



&lt;p&gt;Copiamos el &lt;strong&gt;Application (client) ID&lt;/strong&gt;, que el frontend usará para identificarse ante Entra, y luego entramos a &lt;strong&gt;Authentication (Preview)&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 25]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F18acfkbzjcy9qs97a0di.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F18acfkbzjcy9qs97a0di.png" alt="Imagen 25" width="800" height="476"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 25



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Authentication (Preview)&lt;/strong&gt; vamos a la pestaña &lt;strong&gt;Settings&lt;/strong&gt; y dejamos sin marcar las dos casillas de implicit grant. El Front-channel logout URL también queda vacío, porque solo sirve para cerrar sesión en varias apps a la vez. [Imagen 26]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Frqg4lci0004vq0y04ett.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Frqg4lci0004vq0y04ett.png" alt="Imagen 26" width="800" height="524"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 26



&lt;p&gt;Entramos a &lt;strong&gt;Token configuration&lt;/strong&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add optional claim&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 27]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F7b9osbk1xhzuoceyx30a.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F7b9osbk1xhzuoceyx30a.png" alt="Imagen 27" width="800" height="506"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 27



&lt;p&gt;Elegimos el tipo &lt;em&gt;ID&lt;/em&gt;, marcamos &lt;code&gt;login_hint&lt;/code&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add&lt;/strong&gt;. Con este claim, al cerrar sesión Entra ya no nos pregunta de qué cuenta queremos salir, porque ya sabe cuál es. El claim queda en la lista con tipo ID. [Imagen 28]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnasydjloevmhnujjcvuz.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnasydjloevmhnujjcvuz.png" alt="Imagen 28" width="800" height="628"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 28



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;API permissions&lt;/strong&gt; le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add a permission&lt;/strong&gt;. En el panel que se abre vamos a la pestaña &lt;strong&gt;APIs my organization uses&lt;/strong&gt; y elegimos &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-api&lt;/code&gt;. [Imagen 29]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbxt3lhigmt6ig7rgr74d.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbxt3lhigmt6ig7rgr74d.png" alt="Imagen 29" width="800" height="389"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 29



&lt;p&gt;Elegimos &lt;strong&gt;Delegated permissions&lt;/strong&gt; (la app llama a la API en nombre del usuario que inició sesión). Marcamos &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.Read&lt;/code&gt; y &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.ReadWrite&lt;/code&gt;, que son los scopes que creamos en la API, y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add permissions&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 30]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxnzqexe1ifo358gm5ala.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxnzqexe1ifo358gm5ala.png" alt="Imagen 30" width="800" height="583"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 30



&lt;p&gt;Volvemos a darle a &lt;strong&gt;Add a permission&lt;/strong&gt;, pero esta vez nos quedamos en la pestaña &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft APIs&lt;/strong&gt; y elegimos &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Graph&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 31]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ft7rnmxj5iboqe8vma0vm.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ft7rnmxj5iboqe8vma0vm.png" alt="Imagen 31" width="800" height="394"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 31



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Delegated permissions&lt;/strong&gt; marcamos &lt;code&gt;openid&lt;/code&gt; (iniciar sesión) y &lt;code&gt;offline_access&lt;/code&gt; (renovar la sesión sin volver a pedir el login), y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add permissions&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 32]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F1yydlu7swkpv4pabhajo.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F1yydlu7swkpv4pabhajo.png" alt="Imagen 32" width="799" height="614"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 32



&lt;p&gt;Le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Grant admin consent for Blurlink Demo&lt;/strong&gt; y confirmamos con &lt;strong&gt;Yes&lt;/strong&gt;. En un tenant External los usuarios no pueden aceptar los permisos que pide el frontend, así que el admin los acepta por todos. Sin este paso, Entra no le da el token al frontend. [Imagen 33]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnarki928636z6cjas6l1.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnarki928636z6cjas6l1.png" alt="Imagen 33" width="800" height="436"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 33



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explicación:&lt;/strong&gt; El frontend pide el token a Entra enviándole el scope &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.Read&lt;/code&gt;. Entra necesita que el usuario haya dado su consentimiento para que el frontend tenga ese permiso (scope), pero como el usuario no puede darlo, el admin ya lo aceptó antes por todos los usuarios. Entra verifica eso y le entrega el token al frontend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Con &lt;strong&gt;Refresh&lt;/strong&gt;, todos los permisos quedan en estado Granted. [Imagen 34]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fb1qksu7jgkv39ef4vpqm.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fb1qksu7jgkv39ef4vpqm.png" alt="Imagen 34" width="800" height="427"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 34



&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Crear el user flow
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El user flow define la página de registro e inicio de sesión. Ahí se elige con qué se entra y qué datos se le piden al usuario. En el menú de la izquierda entramos a &lt;strong&gt;External Identities&lt;/strong&gt;, abrimos &lt;strong&gt;User flows&lt;/strong&gt; y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;New user flow&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 35]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fo0hfuusesdb8mxe6vyg8.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fo0hfuusesdb8mxe6vyg8.png" alt="Imagen 35" width="800" height="551"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 35



&lt;p&gt;Le ponemos de nombre &lt;code&gt;SignUpSignIn&lt;/code&gt;, que no se puede cambiar después. En &lt;strong&gt;Identity providers&lt;/strong&gt; elegimos &lt;em&gt;Email with password&lt;/em&gt;; la otra opción, &lt;em&gt;Email one-time passcode&lt;/em&gt;, manda un código al correo en vez de usar contraseña. En &lt;strong&gt;User attributes&lt;/strong&gt; marcamos &lt;em&gt;Given Name&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Surname&lt;/em&gt; y &lt;em&gt;Display Name&lt;/em&gt;; &lt;em&gt;Email Address&lt;/em&gt; ya viene incluido. Le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Create&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 36]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqizebw18lucbtfegoldq.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqizebw18lucbtfegoldq.png" alt="Imagen 36" width="800" height="593"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 36



&lt;p&gt;El user flow aparece en la lista y entramos a él. [Imagen 37]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnz0etb04ux9c3s5sn3f1.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnz0etb04ux9c3s5sn3f1.png" alt="Imagen 37" width="800" height="521"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 37



&lt;p&gt;En &lt;strong&gt;Applications&lt;/strong&gt; le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Add application&lt;/strong&gt;. [Imagen 38]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fmtglmmrld8pi7la12e6k.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fmtglmmrld8pi7la12e6k.png" alt="Imagen 38" width="799" height="480"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 38



&lt;p&gt;Elegimos &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-spa&lt;/code&gt; (nuestro frontend) y le damos a &lt;strong&gt;Select&lt;/strong&gt;. Solo agregamos el SPA, porque es el que muestra el login; la API solo valida tokens. [Imagen 39]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Frnqd7rb6ooe27nijizjo.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Frnqd7rb6ooe27nijizjo.png" alt="Imagen 39" width="800" height="558"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 39



&lt;p&gt;El SPA queda asociado al &lt;em&gt;user flow&lt;/em&gt;; sin esto, el login da error. Aquí también vemos el &lt;strong&gt;Application (client) ID&lt;/strong&gt; del SPA, el mismo que anotamos antes. [Imagen 40]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fvwcv8jfph0yex1f1ptjt.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fvwcv8jfph0yex1f1ptjt.png" alt="Imagen 40" width="800" height="471"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 40



&lt;p&gt;Con esto terminamos la configuración en el portal. Ahora haremos un resumen de los datos importantes de la configuración, que necesitaremos para conectar el frontend, el backend y Entra.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;TENANT (EXTERNAL)
name: Blurlink Demo
subdomain: blurlinkdemo
tenantId: xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxff6e

BACKEND (API)
name: blurlink-demo-api
clientId: xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxx708b
scope: Blurlinks.Read

FRONTEND (SPA)
name: blurlink-demo-spa
clientId: xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxx88ce
redirectUri: http://localhost:5173/redirect
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  6. Repositorios del frontend y del backend
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esta guía se centra en la configuración de Entra External ID, por lo que no entraremos en los detalles del código. Esta sección solo nos permitirá terminar el flujo y comprobar que la configuración realizada funciona.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El frontend se construyó en React con MSAL, la librería de Microsoft que nos permitirá conectarnos a Entra. Con el client ID de &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-spa&lt;/code&gt;, el subdominio y el tenant ID podremos registrarnos e iniciar sesión en la página de Entra que configuramos en el &lt;em&gt;user flow&lt;/em&gt;, y con el scope &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.Read&lt;/code&gt; de &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-api&lt;/code&gt; obtendremos el token para el backend. Gracias a la ruta &lt;code&gt;/redirect&lt;/code&gt; que registramos, Entra nos devolverá a nuestra web.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El backend, construido en NestJS, solo recibirá el access token que le mande el frontend y lo validará con el subdominio, el tenant ID y el client ID de la API (&lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-api&lt;/code&gt;). Si el token es válido, responderá a las consultas HTTP siempre que el token traiga el permiso que pide cada endpoint, como &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.Read&lt;/code&gt; en &lt;code&gt;GET /me&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frontend: &lt;a href="https://github.com/basiliok/demo-fe-entra-external-id-blurlink" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/basiliok/demo-fe-entra-external-id-blurlink&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Backend: &lt;a href="https://github.com/basiliok/demo-be-entra-external-id-blurlink" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/basiliok/demo-be-entra-external-id-blurlink&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nota:&lt;/strong&gt; En cada repositorio se explica cómo levantar el proyecto en su &lt;code&gt;README.md&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Este video muestra la configuración funcionando. Nos registramos, la app nos da la bienvenida, cerramos sesión y al final el nuevo usuario aparece en nuestro tenant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  &lt;iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/YLqlKHvhSuQ" width="710" height="399"&gt;
  &lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nota:&lt;/strong&gt; No hace falta desplegar el frontend ni el backend para probar la configuración de Entra External ID, porque Entra nunca llama a nuestras aplicaciones. Todo el flujo pasa por el navegador, así que el redirect URI solo tiene que estar registrado, no tiene que ser accesible desde internet (por eso sirve &lt;code&gt;http://localhost&lt;/code&gt;). Si desplegamos, solo debemos agregar a los redirect URIs de &lt;code&gt;blurlink-demo-spa&lt;/code&gt; la URL de producción con la ruta, por ejemplo &lt;code&gt;https://tu-dominio.com/redirect&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  7. Cómo funciona el flujo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Este diagrama muestra cómo trabajan juntos el usuario, el frontend, Entra y el backend, desde el registro o el inicio de sesión hasta el mensaje de bienvenida. Y no lo dibujó la IA, tuve que hacerlo yo. ¿Saben cuánto me tomó? ¿Lo saben? Mátenme.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fymwiyzr38owfqiv8jbdb.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fymwiyzr38owfqiv8jbdb.png" alt="Imagen 41" width="799" height="470"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Imagen 41



&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;El usuario elige iniciar sesión o registrarse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;El frontend lo lleva a la página de Entra.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;El usuario escribe su email y su contraseña. Si se registra, también su nombre, su apellido y el código que le llega para verificar su correo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entra revisa los datos y, si es un registro, crea la cuenta.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entra devuelve al usuario a &lt;code&gt;/redirect&lt;/code&gt; con un código. El frontend lo lleva a &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; y ahí le pide a Entra los tokens del inicio de sesión a cambio de ese código.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Esos tokens no sirven para llamar al backend. Por eso, sin que el usuario lo note, el frontend le pide a Entra otro token, solo para el backend, y lo manda junto con &lt;code&gt;GET /me&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Si el backend aún no tiene las llaves públicas de Entra, o las pidió hace más de 10 minutos, se las pide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entra le entrega las llaves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Con esas llaves, el backend comprueba que el token esté firmado por Entra, que lo haya emitido nuestro tenant, que sea para esta API, que no haya vencido y que traiga el permiso &lt;code&gt;Blurlinks.Read&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;El backend devuelve los datos del usuario, y el frontend los muestra junto con un mensaje de bienvenida.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ohhh, se acabó, qué pena. En serio, espero que les sirva. Me hubiera encantado continuar configurando el inicio de sesión con una cuenta de Google (que desde este punto es fácil), pero si no empiezo a buscar trabajo pronto, terminaré haciendo landing pages en WordPress. Hasta la próxima, amiguitos. 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PD: La introducción fue solo una broma.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My &lt;code&gt;/projects&lt;/code&gt; page in Next.js 16 shipped 854 KB of HTML for a list of 49 projects. Almost all of that weight was the same few strings repeated, and in the App Router every repeat ships twice: once as HTML and once more inside the inline React Server Components payload (the &lt;code&gt;self.__next_f.push&lt;/code&gt; scripts at the bottom of the page). Three changes took it to 459 KB: an SVG sprite for the icon on every row, JSON-LD that links to detail pages instead of copying them, and named Tailwind utilities for the row classes. A fourth stopped the page from prefetching 36 routes it didn't need.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why is my Next.js page HTML so large?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open view-source on any App Router page and scroll to the bottom. After the HTML you will find &lt;code&gt;self.__next_f.push([1,"..."])&lt;/code&gt; scripts. That is the RSC payload, the serialized component tree React uses to hydrate the page and to navigate without a full reload. Every element a server component renders appears in it as data, props included.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So a server component that renders an inline &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;svg&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; 49 times puts that path in the document 98 times. On my page today the payload is 261 KB of the 460 KB document.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Compression hides this. The live page is 33 KB with brotli and 45 KB with gzip, because repeated strings are what compressors handle best. That is why the problem never showed up as a slow download. The phone still has to decompress, parse and hold every byte, and that cost lands on the main thread of the slowest device that opens the page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How do I find what is making the page heavy?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Weigh it by parts before changing anything. My first guess was the usual one, large props passed into client components and duplicated into the payload. Every component on &lt;code&gt;/projects&lt;/code&gt; was a server component, so that guess was wrong, and work planned around it would have saved nothing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This script fetches a page and prints the HTML size, the RSC payload, the JSON-LD, and the long attribute values that repeat most:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// weigh.mjs: node weigh.mjs https://example.com/page&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;argv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kb&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${(n / 1024).toFixed(0)} KB`&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flight&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchAll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;__next_f&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"([\s\S]*?)"&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jsonLd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchAll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"application\/ld\+json"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="no"&gt;S&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`HTML ${kb(html.length)}, RSC payload ${kb(flight)}, JSON-LD ${kb(jsonLd)}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Long SVG paths and class strings, in the HTML (d="…") and the payload (\"d\":\"…\").&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;counts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchAll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt;\&lt;span class="n"&gt;bd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;\\&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"?[=:]\\?"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"\\]{80,})/g)) {
  counts.set(m[1], (counts.get(m[1]) ?? 0) + 1)
}
;[...counts]
  .map(([value, n]) =&amp;gt; ({ n, bytes: n * value.length, value: value.slice(0, 50) }))
  .sort((a, b) =&amp;gt; b.bytes - a.bytes)
  .slice(0, 5)
  .forEach((r) =&amp;gt; console.log(`${kb(r.bytes).padStart(7)}  ${String(r.n).padStart(3)}x  ${r.value}…`))
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On the 854 KB version the top line was a single 2,115-character path, the GitHub mark, 98 times.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Fix 1: draw repeated icons once with an SVG sprite
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The GitHub link on each row rendered its own &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;svg&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; with the full path. I moved the paths into one hidden sprite rendered by the root layout, and every icon now points at it with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;use&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;SYMBOLS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;github&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'0 0 438.549 438.549'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'M409.132 114.573c…'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;symbolIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;keyof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;SYMBOLS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SymbolIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SVGProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SVGSVGElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;SYMBOLS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"currentColor"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`#icon-${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;IconSprite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"true"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"0"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"0"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'absolute'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;overflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'hidden'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;entries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;SYMBOLS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;symbol&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`icon-${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"currentColor"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;symbol&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;IconSprite /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; goes once in &lt;code&gt;app/layout.tsx&lt;/code&gt;. Each use is now under 200 bytes instead of 2.1 KB, and &lt;code&gt;currentColor&lt;/code&gt; still follows the link's text colour. &lt;code&gt;/projects&lt;/code&gt; went from 854 KB to 676 KB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sprite is not free. It adds about 3 KB to every page, so a page with one GitHub link got slightly heavier. That trade only pays off for icons that repeat. A single logo stays inline.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Fix 2: JSON-LD on a list page should link, not copy
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The page's &lt;code&gt;ItemList&lt;/code&gt; structured data held a full &lt;code&gt;SoftwareApplication&lt;/code&gt; for each of the 49 projects: name, description, image, author, operating system. Each project's own page already publishes that same entity. The list was 40 KB of JSON-LD, shipped twice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Google's &lt;a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/carousel" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;carousel documentation&lt;/a&gt; describes this case as a summary page: list items that point at detail pages carry only &lt;code&gt;position&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;url&lt;/code&gt;. The helper now returns the short form whenever a detail page exists:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;projectListItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;detailUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;detailUrl&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@type'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'ListItem'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;detailUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@type'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'ListItem'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The JSON-LD went from 40 KB to 10 KB, and no entity is described in two places that could drift apart.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Fix 3: name the class strings every row repeats
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each row carried long Tailwind strings for its grid, thumbnail, title, counter, tag and links, and they shipped twice like everything else. In Tailwind v4 a string that repeats down a long list can become a named utility, variants included:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@utility&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;feed-row&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;@apply&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;relative&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flex&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;flex-col&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;gap-3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;border-b&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;border-slate-300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;py-6&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;last&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;border-none&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;grid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;grid-cols-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;200px_1fr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;gap-6&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;py-7&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;lg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;grid-cols-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;240px_1fr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;One catch: if the element's classes go through &lt;code&gt;cn()&lt;/code&gt; (tailwind-merge), keep colours out of the utility. tailwind-merge can't see inside &lt;code&gt;feed-link&lt;/code&gt;, so it won't know that a caller's &lt;code&gt;text-teal-300&lt;/code&gt; should replace the colour inside it. My &lt;code&gt;feed-link&lt;/code&gt; holds layout only, and the colours stay on the element.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To prove nothing changed visually, I compared computed styles for every row part between a local &lt;code&gt;next start&lt;/code&gt; build and production. They matched except for a rounding difference in one oklab channel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fixes 2 and 3 together took the page from 658 KB to 459 KB. (A rebuild between the two passes measured 658 KB, not the 676 KB from the sprite step.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Fix 4: prefetch links on intent, not on scroll
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This one doesn't change the HTML. Next.js prefetches every &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Link&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; as it enters the viewport. On a page with a link per row, one visit to &lt;code&gt;/projects&lt;/code&gt; fired 36 route prefetches, about 1 MB decoded, and on Vercel each one is a CDN request plus ISR reads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Next.js docs suggest a hover-only pattern for this. I added focus and touchstart so keyboard and phone users still get a head start:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'use client'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/link'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;IntentLink&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ComponentProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;intent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setIntent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;prefetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;intent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onMouseEnter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setIntent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onFocus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setIntent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onTouchStart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setIntent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; is the default prefetch behaviour; &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; turns it off until there is intent. The &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a href&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in the HTML is identical, so crawlers see the same links.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How do I keep the page from growing back?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Set a budget that fails. My production check reads every URL in the sitemap and fails any page over 520 KB of uncompressed HTML:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;HTML_BUDGET_KB&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;520&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;kb&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;round&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kb&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;HTML_BUDGET_KB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${url}: ${kb} KB of HTML, budget ${HTML_BUDGET_KB} KB`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And pin each fix with a test. The sprite test renders each repeated icon and fails if one use is over 200 bytes or doesn't reference its symbol.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The budget alone wasn't enough. Writing this article, I ran the weighing script again and found a link arrow drawn inline 82 times on the page, about 11 KB, still under the budget and so never flagged. It is a symbol now too, and the page is 448 KB. So I re-run the weigh script whenever a list page changes, not only when the budget fails.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://tamiz.pro/insights/nextjs-server-side-caching-patterns" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;tamiz.pro&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js 15's App Router ships with four distinct caching layers, and confusing them is the single most common source of stale data, memory leaks, and mysterious 404s in production. This deep dive maps every layer — Request Memoization, the Data Cache, the Full Route Cache, and the Router Cache — then walks through the advanced patterns that actually work in production: tag-based invalidation, &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; with custom keys, time-based revalidation (ISR), and cache-aware streaming. By the end, you'll know exactly which cache is serving a request, why it's serving it, and how to invalidate it deterministically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1. The Four Caching Layers: A Mental Model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2. Layer 1 — Request Memoization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3. Layer 2 — The Data Cache&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4. Layer 3 — The Full Route Cache&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5. Layer 4 — The Router Cache&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6. Advanced Pattern: Tag-Based Revalidation with &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7. Advanced Pattern: &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; with Custom Keys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8. Advanced Pattern: Time-Based Revalidation (ISR) Done Right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9. Advanced Pattern: Cache-Aware Streaming and Suspense&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10. Production Best Practices and Common Pitfalls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequently Asked Questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. The Four Caching Layers: A Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every request in the App Router passes through up to four independent caches. They have different lifetimes, different scopes, and different invalidation triggers. Treating them as one "Next.js cache" is the root of nearly every caching bug.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        Browser (Client)                    │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Layer 4: Router Cache (client-side, ~30s default)    │ │
│  │  Stores RSC payloads for back/forward navigation      │ │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                           │ HTTP request
┌──────────────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐
│                       Next.js Server                        │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Layer 3: Full Route Cache (static HTML per route)    │ │
│  │  Persists the rendered HTML + RSC payload on disk     │ │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Layer 2: Data Cache (persistent, cross-request)      │ │
│  │  Stores fetch() results + unstable_cache output       │ │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Layer 1: Request Memoization (per-request, in-memory)│ │
│  │  Dedupes identical fetch() calls within one render    │ │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Layer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Scope&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Persistence&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Default Lifetime&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Primary Invalidation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Request Memoization&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One render pass&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In-memory&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Request ends&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;None (automatic)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Data Cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Global (server)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Persistent (disk/DB)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; default: 0s (no store); &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt;: infinite&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt;, time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Full Route Cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per-route&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Persistent (disk)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Static routes: infinite&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt;, rebuild, time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Router Cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per-client session&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;In-memory&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;30s (default)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Navigation, &lt;code&gt;router.refresh()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key insight:&lt;/strong&gt; These layers are &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; alternatives. A single page request can be served from the Router Cache, then the Full Route Cache, then the Data Cache, then Request Memoization — in that order. Knowing which one is holding your stale data is step one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Layer 1 — Request Memoization
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Request Memoization is the simplest and least understood layer. During a single server render, Next.js deduplicates identical &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; calls (and wrapped &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; calls) so that a function called twice with the same arguments hits the network once.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/products/[id]/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// If ProductCard and PriceChart both call fetchProduct(id),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the network request happens ONCE per render.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchPrice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductCard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PriceChart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`https://api.example.com/products/${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchPrice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`https://api.example.com/products/${id}/price`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  What it does and doesn't do
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dedupes&lt;/strong&gt; identical &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; URLs + options within a single render pass.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Does NOT persist&lt;/strong&gt; across requests. The next request re-fetches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Does NOT cache&lt;/strong&gt; non-&lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; data. If you query a database with &lt;code&gt;prisma&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;pg&lt;/code&gt;, there is &lt;em&gt;no&lt;/em&gt; memoization unless you wrap it in &lt;code&gt;React.cache()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The &lt;code&gt;React.cache()&lt;/code&gt; escape hatch
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For non-&lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; data sources (DB queries, SDK calls, file reads), you can opt into per-request memoization yourself:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/db.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findUnique&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now &lt;code&gt;getUser('123')&lt;/code&gt; called ten times in one render executes the query once. This is a pure per-request optimization — it never survives the request, so it's safe to use liberally.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Layer 2 — The Data Cache
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Data Cache is the persistent, cross-request cache for &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; results and &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; outputs. This is where most advanced patterns live.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3.1 &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; caching semantics in Next.js 15
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js 15 changed the default: &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;no longer cached&lt;/strong&gt; by default. You must opt in explicitly.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/dashboard/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ NOT cached (Next.js 15 default) — hits the network on every request&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/stats'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ Cached for 60 seconds (stale-while-revalidate)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/stats'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ Cached indefinitely until manually invalidated&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/stats'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'stats'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ Never cached, always fresh&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/stats'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'no-store'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Option&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Behavior&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Typical Use Case&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;em&gt;(none)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No cache (Next 15 default)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Live data, auth-dependent data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;next: { revalidate: N }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stale-while-revalidate, N seconds&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Dashboards, listings&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;next: { tags: [...] }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cache forever until tag invalidated&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CMS content, reference data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;cache: 'no-store'&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bypass entirely&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real-time, user-specific data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;cache: 'force-cache'&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Force cache (legacy behavior)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rare — prefer &lt;code&gt;revalidate&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;tags&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3.2 Stale-while-revalidate (SWR) in the Data Cache
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you set &lt;code&gt;revalidate: 60&lt;/code&gt;, Next.js serves the cached value immediately and triggers a background revalidation in the next request after 60 seconds. Users never wait for the network — they get the previous data, and the fresh data is swapped in on the &lt;em&gt;subsequent&lt;/em&gt; request.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/products/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductsPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 5 minutes&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductGrid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trade-off:&lt;/strong&gt; SWR gives you sub-second TTFB at the cost of serving data that's up to &lt;code&gt;revalidate&lt;/code&gt; seconds old. For a product catalog that's fine. For a stock ticker, it's not.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. Layer 3 — The Full Route Cache
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Full Route Cache stores the &lt;em&gt;rendered HTML&lt;/em&gt; and the RSC payload for statically rendered routes. It's why a static page can be served from a CDN without running any server code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4.1 Static vs. dynamic rendering
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A route is &lt;strong&gt;static&lt;/strong&gt; (and thus eligible for the Full Route Cache) only if every data fetch in it is cacheable. A single &lt;code&gt;cache: 'no-store'&lt;/code&gt; or a &lt;code&gt;cookies()&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;headers()&lt;/code&gt; call makes the whole route &lt;strong&gt;dynamic&lt;/strong&gt;, which disables the Full Route Cache for that route.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/account/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AccountPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ This makes the ENTIRE route dynamic.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// The Full Route Cache is bypassed; every request re-renders.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cookies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`https://api.example.com/users/${session.get('uid')}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'no-store'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Account&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  4.2 Forcing static generation with &lt;code&gt;generateStaticParams&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For dynamic routes, you can pre-render known parameter combinations at build time:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getAllSlugs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@/lib/posts'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateStaticParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;slugs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getAllSlugs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;slugs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;slug&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;slug&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;slug&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`https://api.example.com/posts/${params.slug}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3600&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 1 hour ISR&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;article&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;article&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now &lt;code&gt;/blog/hello-world&lt;/code&gt; is pre-rendered at build time, served from the Full Route Cache, and revalidated every hour — the classic ISR pattern.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Layer 4 — The Router Cache
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Router Cache lives in the browser. It stores the RSC payload of previously visited routes so that back/forward navigation is instant. It's ephemeral (per-client, cleared on refresh) and has a default stale time of 30 seconds.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// next.config.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextConfig&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nextConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextConfig&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;experimental&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;staleTimes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;dynamic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// dynamic routes: never stale-cache&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;180&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// static routes: 3 minutes&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nextConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Common bug:&lt;/strong&gt; You update a database, call &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt;, and the server data is fresh — but the browser still shows stale UI because the Router Cache is serving the old RSC payload. The fix is &lt;code&gt;router.refresh()&lt;/code&gt; after a mutation, or &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;type: 'layout'&lt;/code&gt; to force a full refetch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  6. Advanced Pattern: Tag-Based Revalidation with &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tags are the most powerful invalidation primitive in Next.js. They let you invalidate &lt;em&gt;every&lt;/em&gt; cached fetch tagged with a string, from anywhere — a server action, a route handler, or a webhook — without knowing which route consumed it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  6.1 Tagging fetches
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/products/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductsPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'catalog'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductGrid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  6.2 Invalidating from a Server Action
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/products/actions.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'use server'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;deleteProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;productId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;productId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Every fetch tagged 'products' is now stale.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// The next request to /products will re-fetch from the origin.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  6.3 Invalidating from a webhook (route handler)
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/api/webhooks/cms/route.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextResponse&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/server'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Validate the webhook signature...&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isValidSignature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Unauthorized'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;401&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Invalidate the affected content — no need to know which pages use it.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;entityType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// e.g. 'blog-post', 'product'&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  6.4 The composite tag pattern
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tag with both a &lt;em&gt;collection&lt;/em&gt; and a &lt;em&gt;single item&lt;/em&gt; so you can invalidate granularly or broadly:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/data.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;API&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${API}/products/${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`product-${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${API}/products`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/products/[id]/actions.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'use server'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;updateProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Invalidate just this product AND the whole list.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`product-${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now updating one product refreshes its detail page and the listing page, but leaves other product detail pages untouched.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  7. Advanced Pattern: &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; with Custom Keys
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; only caches HTTP requests. For database queries, external SDK calls, or computed values, you need &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; — the official escape hatch for arbitrary async functions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  7.1 The basic wrapper
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/analytics.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getDailyRevenue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;startDate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;endDate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Any async work: Prisma, Drizzle, an SDK, a file read...&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;groupBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;by&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'date'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;gte&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;startDate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lte&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;endDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;_sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Cache key parts — must be serializable.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'daily-revenue'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Options&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 15 minutes&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'analytics'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'revenue'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  7.2 The critical gotcha: arguments are NOT part of the key
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; uses only the &lt;em&gt;key parts array&lt;/em&gt; to build the cache entry. The function's arguments are ignored for keying purposes. If you call &lt;code&gt;getDailyRevenue('2025-01-01', '2025-01-31')&lt;/code&gt; and then &lt;code&gt;getDailyRevenue('2025-02-01', '2025-02-28')&lt;/code&gt;, both calls return the &lt;strong&gt;same cached result&lt;/strong&gt; unless you include the arguments in the key.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ WRONG — both calls share one cache entry&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getRevenue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;queryRevenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'revenue'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;900&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRevenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-01-01'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-01-31'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// caches under ['revenue']&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRevenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-02-01'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-02-28'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ returns January's data!&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ CORRECT — include the args in the key parts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getRevenue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;queryRevenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'revenue'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// dynamic key function&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;900&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRevenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-01-01'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-01-31'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// caches under ['revenue', '2025-01-01', '2025-01-31']&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRevenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-02-01'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2025-02-28'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ separate entry&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The key function receives the same arguments as the wrapped function and must return a serializable array. This is the #1 source of subtle bugs with &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  7.3 Combining &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;React.cache()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use both for maximum safety: &lt;code&gt;React.cache()&lt;/code&gt; dedupes within a request; &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; persists across requests.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/user.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;_getUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findUnique&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`user-${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'users'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3600&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_getUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now the same user fetched in ten components during one render hits the cache once, and the cached result survives across requests for an hour.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  8. Advanced Pattern: Time-Based Revalidation (ISR) Done Right
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) is the time-based counterpart to tag-based invalidation. It's ideal when you can tolerate up to N seconds of staleness but want zero server load on the critical path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  8.1 Per-fetch revalidation vs. per-route revalidation
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can set revalidation at the fetch level (as we've seen) or at the route level via the &lt;code&gt;revalidate&lt;/code&gt; export. Route-level revalidation applies to &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; fetches in the route that don't specify their own.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/blog/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Applies to every fetch in this route unless overridden.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 1 hour&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BlogPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/posts'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// inherits 3600&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostList&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  8.2 On-demand revalidation with &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Time-based ISR is passive. When you need to invalidate &lt;em&gt;immediately&lt;/em&gt; (e.g. a user publishes a post), use &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/admin/actions.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'use server'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;publishPost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;postId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;postId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;published&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Revalidate the post page and the blog index immediately.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`/blog/${postId}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'/blog'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  8.3 The hybrid pattern: time + tags
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For most real apps, combine both: use tags for deterministic invalidation, and set a generous &lt;code&gt;revalidate&lt;/code&gt; as a safety net so stale data self-heals even if a webhook fails.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;getProduct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchProductFromDb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`product-${id}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;86400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 24h safety net&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'catalog'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This gives you: instant invalidation via webhooks/actions, plus automatic recovery within 24 hours if something goes wrong. This is the pattern I recommend for most production CMS-driven sites.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  9. Advanced Pattern: Cache-Aware Streaming and Suspense
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Streaming with Suspense changes how caching behaves. When a route is static and you stream a component, the Full Route Cache stores the &lt;em&gt;initial&lt;/em&gt; HTML shell and the &lt;em&gt;entire&lt;/em&gt; RSC payload — including the streamed content — so the second visit is instant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  9.1 Streaming a cached fetch
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/dashboard/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;DashboardPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Skeleton&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RevenueChart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Skeleton&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RecentOrders&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RevenueChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// This fetch is cached. The component streams in, but the RSC payload&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// is stored in the Full Route Cache so the next visit is instant.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/revenue'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'revenue'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Chart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  9.2 The &lt;code&gt;dynamic&lt;/code&gt; export — controlling the whole route
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes you need to force a route out of the Full Route Cache entirely (e.g. an admin dashboard showing live data). Use the &lt;code&gt;dynamic&lt;/code&gt; export:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/admin/overview/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Force dynamic rendering — bypasses Full Route Cache for this route.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dynamic&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'force-dynamic'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AdminOverview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stats&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://api.example.com/admin/stats'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'no-store'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;StatsPanel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stats&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;stats&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule of thumb:&lt;/strong&gt; Use &lt;code&gt;force-dynamic&lt;/code&gt; sparingly. It disables &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; static optimization for the route, including the shell, which can tank performance on high-traffic pages. Prefer per-fetch &lt;code&gt;no-store&lt;/code&gt; or short &lt;code&gt;revalidate&lt;/code&gt; values instead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  10. Production Best Practices and Common Pitfalls
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  10.1 Pitfall: The Router Cache is the invisible culprit
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You call &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt;, your server data is fresh, but the UI doesn't update. That's the Router Cache serving a stale RSC payload. Fix: call &lt;code&gt;router.refresh()&lt;/code&gt; after mutations, or set &lt;code&gt;staleTimes.dynamic: 0&lt;/code&gt; for routes that must always be fresh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  10.2 Pitfall: &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; key collisions
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Forgetting to include function arguments in the cache key causes cross-argument data bleed. Always use the dynamic key function form when the function takes arguments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  10.3 Pitfall: Mixing &lt;code&gt;no-store&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;revalidate&lt;/code&gt; in one route
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A single &lt;code&gt;no-store&lt;/code&gt; fetch makes the whole route dynamic and disables the Full Route Cache — even if other fetches are cached. This silently kills ISR. Check the Network tab: if the route responds with &lt;code&gt;x-nextjs-cache: no-store&lt;/code&gt;, you've been bitten.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  10.4 Best practice: Centralize cache configuration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Define your cache policies in one place so you can tune them without hunting through components:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/cache-policies.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;CACHE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;cms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'cms'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;analytics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'analytics'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'session'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;catalog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'catalog'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'products'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Usage:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;CACHE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;catalog&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  10.5 Best practice: Log cache hits and misses in development
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/with-cache-log.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'next/cache'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;withCacheLog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Parameters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nb"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`[cache:miss] ${key.join('/')}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Log when the cache is populated after a miss&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;revalidate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  10.6 Best practice: Use &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt; for page-level, &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt; for data-level
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt; is coarse — it invalidates the Full Route Cache for a path and everything nested. &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt; is fine-grained — it invalidates only the data tagged. Prefer tags for data that's shared across many routes; use paths only when you want to force a full page re-render.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Frequently Asked Questions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Q: Why is my &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; not being cached even though I set &lt;code&gt;next: { revalidate: 60 }&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A: Check three things. First, make sure the route isn't dynamic — a &lt;code&gt;cookies()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;headers()&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;searchParams&lt;/code&gt; read forces dynamic rendering, which disables the Full Route Cache but &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; the Data Cache. Second, verify you're not passing &lt;code&gt;cache: 'no-store'&lt;/code&gt; anywhere in the same route, which makes the whole route dynamic. Third, confirm the fetch URL is a full absolute URL — relative URLs are not cached. Inspect the response headers: &lt;code&gt;x-nextjs-cache: HIT&lt;/code&gt; confirms the Data Cache served it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Q: What's the difference between &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A: &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt; invalidates the Full Route Cache for a specific path and all nested routes — it forces a re-render of those pages. &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt; invalidates the Data Cache entries tagged with that string, which can span many routes. Use &lt;code&gt;revalidateTag&lt;/code&gt; for data shared across routes (e.g. a CMS collection), and &lt;code&gt;revalidatePath&lt;/code&gt; when you want to guarantee a specific page's HTML is regenerated. In practice, you'll often call both.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Q: Is &lt;code&gt;unstable_cache&lt;/code&gt; safe to use in production?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A: Yes, it's widely used in production, but the API is still marked unstable and may change in future majors. The main risk is the key-collision pitfall described in Section 7.2 — always use the dynamic key function when your wrapped function takes arguments. For a stable alternative, consider the &lt;code&gt;use cache&lt;/code&gt; directive (experimental in Next.js 15) which brings compiler-level caching and is expected to become the standard. For more on the evolution of these APIs, see &lt;a href="https://tamiz.pro/insights" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Tamiz's Insights&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I opened a budget app last month to check one number, how much I had left to spend, and I could not find it. The balance was on one screen, the spending was on another, and the budget was a third screen with a tiny progress bar I had to squint at. I knew the data was in there somewhere, the app had it, it just was not showing me. I closed it and did the math in my head instead, which is the exact moment a UI has failed at its job.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I keep coming back to a line from &lt;a href="https://dev.to/dailycontext/ask-more-of-your-ui-2nf7"&gt;Ben Halpern's post, ask more of your UI&lt;/a&gt;. The idea is simple: a UI should act like an instrument panel, showing you what is going on, live, instead of hiding the state behind taps and menus. A car dashboard does not make you open a menu to see your speed. It is just there, all the time, because the whole point of the dashboard is to tell you where you stand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built a little budget tracker to try the idea out, nothing fancy, just a panel that shows the four things I actually check. Balance, spent this month against the budget, the next bill coming up, and whether the data is synced. Every number updates the moment something changes, so the panel is always current. Here is the version the demo below runs, with buttons to add an expense and watch the numbers move.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try it: a budget panel that talks back&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Try it live on &lt;a href="https://nayemalam.com/blog/ui-should-tell-you-whats-going-on" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;nayemalam.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  the quiet UI vs the panel
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The quiet version of this app is the one I opened last month. It has the same data, but it shows you almost none of it. You tap through three screens to assemble the picture yourself, and by the time you have, you have forgotten why you opened the app. The panel version puts the four numbers on one screen and keeps them current. Nothing about it is clever, and that is the point. The clever part would be hiding the numbers behind a gesture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The pattern shows up everywhere once you start looking for it. A form that tells you the password is too short while you type, instead of after you submit. A file upload that shows progress and a real error message, instead of a spinner that just keeps spinning. A settings page that says when it last synced, instead of leaving you to wonder whether your change saved. In every case, the fix is the same: surface the state, keep it live, and let the user see it without asking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  the cost is real, and small
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The objection I hear is that showing more state means more code, and more code means more bugs. That is fair, and it is also mostly wrong at this scale. The budget panel is a handful of &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; calls and a progress bar. The state already exists in the app, it is the same state the quiet version hides. The work is not computing the numbers, it is deciding to render them. The extra code is a few lines of JSX, and the payoff is that the user stops doing mental math to fill in the blanks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Where I draw the line is noise. An instrument panel is not a firehose. A car dashboard shows speed, fuel, and warnings, not the raw sensor feed. The budget panel shows four numbers, not every transaction since 2019. The test I use is whether the number changes a decision. Balance changes whether I buy something. Spent-against-budget changes whether I cook tonight. Sync status changes whether I trust the numbers at all. If a number would not change a decision, it does not earn a spot on the panel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What I took away from building the panel is that showing state is a design choice, not a feature. The data was always there. The quiet app had it and hid it. The panel just decided the user is allowed to see it. I check the budget app more now, not because I enjoy budgeting, but because opening it answers the question in one glance instead of three taps. A UI exists to tell you what is going on, and the ones that do it well feel less like software and more like a dashboard you can trust.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally posted on &lt;a href="https://nayemalam.com/blog/ui-should-tell-you-whats-going-on" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;nayemalam.com/blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first version of the &lt;a href="https://tryseatfinder.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;SeatFinder&lt;/a&gt; seating chart was one long flat list. Eighty guests, each row with a name and a table number in parentheses, sorted by table. It worked, technically. It also looked like a spreadsheet that had lost its will to live, and finding your own table meant scanning the whole page. A seating chart is not a list of guests. It is a list of tables, and each table has its own list of guests, and the page should look like that.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix was a &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/map" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; inside a &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;. It felt weird the first time I wrote it, like I was nesting something that should stay flat, and I spent a while wondering if there was a cleaner way. There is not, really. When the data is nested, the render is nested, and the cleanest version is the one that admits it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  the shape of the data decides the shape of the render
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The data already had the answer in it. Each table is an object with a guests array inside it, because that is how a wedding actually works. Nobody thinks of a seating chart as eighty loose guests. They think of it as ten tables with eight people each.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;seating-data.ts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Guest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'t1'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Table 1'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'g1'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Sarah Chen'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'g2'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Michael Okafor'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'t2'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Table 2'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'g3'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Amira Yusuf'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'g4'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Jon Park'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Once the data looks like that, the component almost writes itself. The outer &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; turns each table into a section, and the inner &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; turns each guest into a row inside that section. Two levels of data, two levels of &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;, and the JSX mirrors the shape of the thing it is showing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SeatingChart.tsx&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SeatingChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That is the pattern, and it generalizes further than seating charts. A file browser is folders with files inside. A comment thread is comments with replies inside. A settings page is sections with options inside. Any time the screen shows groups with items in them, the render is a &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; inside a &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;, whether you write it that way or fight it with a flattened list and a bunch of conditional headers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  the key rule applies twice
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The part I got wrong the first time was the &lt;a href="https://react.dev/learn/rendering-lists#keeping-list-items-in-order-with-key" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. I put one on the outer &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; and forgot the inner one, and React answered with the warning every React developer has seen at least once: each child in a list should have a unique key. The fix is obvious once you say it out loud. There are two lists here, so there are two &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; props, one on each level.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One detail that surprised me: an inner &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; only has to be unique among its siblings, not across the whole page. Two guests named Sarah at two different tables can both have the id &lt;code&gt;g1&lt;/code&gt; in their own lists and React is fine with it, because each &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; is its own list. In practice I still use globally unique ids, because a guest moves between tables and I want the id to follow the person, but the rule itself is per list, not per page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The index-as-key trap is worse in nested lists than in flat ones, because there are two indexes to get wrong. If a guest moves from Table 1 to Table 2, and both lists are keyed by index, React sees the same keys in the same positions and keeps the old state on the wrong rows. I learned this one from a checkbox. A guest checked in at Table 1, I moved them to Table 2, and the checkmark stayed behind on the person who took their seat. The checkbox belonged to the row, not the guest, because the key said so. Stable ids on both levels fixed it, and it has stayed fixed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Try it: nested maps, live, with real keys&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Try it live on &lt;a href="https://nayemalam.com/blog/map-within-a-map" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;nayemalam.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check a few guests in, then hit reverse table order. The checkmarks travel with the guests, because each row is keyed by a stable id, on both levels of the nesting. Key by index instead and the checkmarks would stay glued to their rows while the names moved around them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  when the inner map deserves its own component
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A nested &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; reads fine at two levels. At three, the JSX starts to look like a staircase, and the indentation is telling you something. The usual fix is to pull the inner &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; out into its own component, which also gives the inner list a name, and named things are easier to think about than anonymous blocks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SeatingChart.tsx&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TableGuests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SeatingChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TableGuests&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I do this when the inner list has any logic of its own, sorting, a checked-in state, an empty state for a table with no guests yet. If the inner &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; is just turning items into rows, leaving it inline is fine. The rule I use is the same one I use everywhere else: extract when the block has a name and a reason to exist on its own, not before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  the flat alternative, for when the grouping is only visual
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes the nesting is in the data but the screen does not need it. A search box over all guests, for example, does not care which table anyone sits at. Flattening first, then mapping once, is the honest version of that. &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/flatMap" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;flatMap&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the method for it: &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; plus one level of flattening, so &lt;code&gt;tables.flatMap((table) =&amp;gt; table.guests)&lt;/code&gt; gives you one flat array of every guest, and a single &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; renders them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;all-guests.ts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;allGuests&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tables&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;flatMap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nb"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;allGuests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 4, every guest from every table, in one flat list&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The choice is about what the screen is showing. Grouped on screen, nested &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;. One continuous list on screen, flatten first and map once. I reach for the nested version more often than I expected, because most grouped data wants to stay grouped where the user can see it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What I took away from the seating chart is that the render should follow the data, not fight it. Nested data gets a nested &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt;, a &lt;em&gt;&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/em&gt; on every level, and stable ids instead of indexes, especially when items can move between groups. The flat list I started with was not simpler, it was just the same complexity with the structure hidden, and the moment the page needed to look like a seating chart, the nested version was the one that already did.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally posted on &lt;a href="https://nayemalam.com/blog/map-within-a-map" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;nayemalam.com/blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I merged three pull requests today. A data table post, a retitle, and another retitle, all on the portfolio repo. Every one of them followed the same little ritual. Open the PR, scroll past the description, scroll past the comments, keep scrolling, and somewhere near the bottom, find the merge box and check whether it is green. I do that over and over across four repos, and it always felt backwards, like checking whether the front door is locked by walking to the back of the house first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; shipped a redesigned Overview page on November 5, as an opt-in public preview, and it moves the answer to the top. The merge box is now a compact readiness summary pinned near the top of the PR, showing merge status, checks, comments, approvals, and what to do next, all in under half the space the old merge box took. You can read the full announcement in the &lt;a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-05-new-pull-request-overview-page-in-public-preview/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;changelog&lt;/a&gt;. Rollout is continuing through the weekend, so some accounts may not see the option right away.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fkc3j678uftvcjlmed0u5.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fkc3j678uftvcjlmed0u5.png" alt="GitHub screenshot of the new pull request Overview page, with the merge readiness summary, checks, comments, approvals, and recent activity at the top" width="800" height="420"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fzf92t0ty2z7brug0mwg6.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fzf92t0ty2z7brug0mwg6.png" alt="GitHub screenshot comparing the classic merge box with the compact readiness summary" width="800" height="417"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  what else moved
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The summary is the headline, but the conversation got tools too. You can filter comments to All, Unresolved, or Mine, so you can jump straight to the open questions or your own feedback instead of re-reading the whole thread. You can sort newest first instead of only chronological, which is the order I actually want when I come back to a PR I already read. There is an activity summary in the upper right for review comments, review requests, and other updates. And marking a draft ready for review or closing a PR moved into the page header, with the same permissions as before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk3rtf9pw4p3oap95c0py.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk3rtf9pw4p3oap95c0py.png" alt="GitHub screenshot of pull request comments with All, Unresolved, and Mine filters, newest-first sorting, and a summary of recent activity" width="800" height="482"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  what did not change
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nothing under the hood. Branch protection rules, required status checks, required reviewers, merge queues, and the PR API and webhooks all behave exactly as before. This is a layout change, not a merge-rules change, which is why I am comfortable turning it on. The worst case is I do not like the layout, and I switch back to classic from the same menu, because the preview lets you go back at any time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  part of a longer redesign
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Overview page is the next piece of a PR redesign GitHub has been working through all year. In March a new pulls dashboard entered public preview with an inbox and saved views, and by April it moved to opt-out. The Overview page is the same idea applied to the single PR view. GitHub calls this preview a starting point, not the finished experience, and they are collecting feedback in &lt;a href="https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/212186" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Community Discussion #212186&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test for me is simple. The next time I open a long PR, do I know whether it can merge before I scroll? If the answer is yes, the redesign did its job. If I still catch myself scrolling to double-check, I will switch back to classic and say so in the feedback thread, because GitHub asked for exactly that kind of answer.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally posted on &lt;a href="https://nayemalam.com/blog/github-new-pr-overview" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;nayemalam.com/blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Meet Lenso UI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bringing the design language and interactions of iOS and iPadOS to the web.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Glass materials. Elastic feedback. Fluid menus.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Built with Base UI + StyleX.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Try it: &lt;a href="https://ui.lenso.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://ui.lenso.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Source: &lt;a href="https://github.com/LioRael/lenso-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/LioRael/lenso-ui&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I spent the last couple of weeks building a website template for dental clinics, mostly to learn the Next.js 16 App Router properly: static rendering with &lt;code&gt;next-intl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;next/og&lt;/code&gt;, the new &lt;code&gt;proxy.ts&lt;/code&gt;, Tailwind 4. The free version is MIT on GitHub, the full one has booking, a gallery and a second language.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lite (MIT): &lt;a href="https://github.com/aivnaov123/lumen-dental-lite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/aivnaov123/lumen-dental-lite&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live demo of the full version: &lt;a href="https://lumen-dental-demo-brown.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://lumen-dental-demo-brown.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are the five things that cost me the most time, so they don't cost you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Every page silently became dynamic
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With &lt;code&gt;next-intl&lt;/code&gt; and a &lt;code&gt;[locale]&lt;/code&gt; segment, I had &lt;code&gt;generateStaticParams&lt;/code&gt; in the layout and assumed everything was prerendered. The build output said otherwise: every route was &lt;code&gt;ƒ (Dynamic)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cause: &lt;code&gt;getLocale()&lt;/code&gt; (and anything that reads the locale) falls back to request headers unless &lt;strong&gt;each page&lt;/strong&gt; calls &lt;code&gt;setRequestLocale(locale)&lt;/code&gt; — the layout alone isn't enough.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ServicesPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setRequestLocale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;copy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getContent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;After adding it to all 11 pages: 30 static pages, 60 ms TTFB on Vercel. Check your build output for &lt;code&gt;●&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;ƒ&lt;/code&gt; — it's easy to miss.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. The root &lt;code&gt;opengraph-image.tsx&lt;/code&gt; 404'd in production
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I put &lt;code&gt;opengraph-image.tsx&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;src/app/&lt;/code&gt;, as the docs show. Locally it worked; on Vercel &lt;code&gt;/opengraph-image&lt;/code&gt; returned 404 and no &lt;code&gt;og:image&lt;/code&gt; tag was emitted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The i18n middleware matcher excluded files with an extension (&lt;code&gt;.*\..*&lt;/code&gt;) — but &lt;code&gt;/opengraph-image&lt;/code&gt; has none, so it was treated as a page and routed to the locale handler.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: move it inside the segment, &lt;code&gt;src/app/[locale]/opengraph-image.tsx&lt;/code&gt;, read &lt;code&gt;params.locale&lt;/code&gt;, and you get a per-language OG image for free:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateStaticParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;locales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;OpenGraphImage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;copy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;contentFor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;locale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ImageResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* ... */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  3. &lt;code&gt;toISOString().slice(0, 10)&lt;/code&gt; lost a day
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The booking calendar stored the selected date as &lt;code&gt;date.toISOString().slice(0, 10)&lt;/code&gt;. In Sofia (UTC+2), clicking Monday the 23rd produced &lt;code&gt;2026-11-22&lt;/code&gt; — Sunday, which the clinic is closed on. Classic, and I still wrote it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;toISODate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pad&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;padStart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${d.getFullYear()}-${pad(d.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(d.getDate())}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Anything that represents a calendar day should never go through UTC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. The hero was invisible until JavaScript loaded
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lighthouse mobile gave the home page a 62. LCP was 4.6 s even though the hero image was 23 KB. The culprit was Framer Motion: &lt;code&gt;initial={{ opacity: 0 }}&lt;/code&gt; on the hero meant the largest element painted only after hydration on a throttled CPU.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two changes took it to 91:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Above the fold, animate &lt;strong&gt;transform only&lt;/strong&gt;, in CSS, so first paint isn't gated on JS:
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;  &lt;span class="k"&gt;@keyframes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;rise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;translateY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;18px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;translateY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Below the fold, keep Framer Motion but load it lazily with &lt;code&gt;LazyMotion&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;m&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;motion&lt;/code&gt; — JS on the home page dropped from 342 KB to 179 KB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also: &lt;code&gt;useSearchParams()&lt;/code&gt; inside &lt;code&gt;Suspense&lt;/code&gt; with an empty fallback made the booking page's footer jump (CLS 0.47). A skeleton with the same height fixed it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Custom 404 never showed
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;[locale]/not-found.tsx&lt;/code&gt; is only rendered when something calls &lt;code&gt;notFound()&lt;/code&gt;. Unknown URLs under a dynamic segment don't — Next served its plain default 404. A catch-all route solves it:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/app/[locale]/[...rest]/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;notFound&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"next/navigation"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CatchAll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;notFound&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  What's in the template
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All copy lives in &lt;code&gt;src/content/&amp;lt;locale&amp;gt;/*.ts&lt;/code&gt;, shared config in &lt;code&gt;src/config/&lt;/code&gt;. Nine services, six doctors, booking with calendar/slots/validation and email or webhook delivery, before/after sliders, financing section, dark mode, EN + BG, schema.org &lt;code&gt;Dentist&lt;/code&gt; JSON-LD, sitemap/robots/manifest. Lighthouse 100 desktop, 90+ mobile.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you build sites for clinics, the full version is a one-time purchase (link in the repo README). If you just want to poke at the Next.js 16 setup, the lite is free — PRs and issues welcome.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Happy to answer questions about any of the above in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  Benchmarking n8n Workflow Execution: Throughput, Memory Overhead, and p99 Latency Under Load
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When evaluating n8n-io/n8n for production workflow automation, the critical question isn't feature count—it's whether the runtime can sustain concurrent executions without degrading response times or exhausting memory. We ran a three-phase load test against a self-hosted n8n instance (v1.23.0, Node.js 20.11, 4-core/8GB VPS) to establish baseline metrics for workflow throughput, memory stability, and latency distribution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Test Topology
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We deployed a load harness using k6 v0.48 with the following configuration:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// k6-n8n-benchmark.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'k6/http'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;check&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sleep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'k6'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;stages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2m'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Ramp-up&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'5m'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Sustained&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2m'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Spike&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'3m'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Hold spike&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'2m'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Ramp-down&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;thresholds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;http_req_duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'p(95)&amp;lt;1500'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'p(99)&amp;lt;3000'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;http_req_failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'rate&amp;lt;0.05'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;workflowId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'test-ai-enrichment'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;__VU&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;timestamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'http://n8n.local:5678/webhook/benchmark'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Content-Type'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'application/json'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;check&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'status is 200'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'execution completed'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'status'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'success'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sleep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The test workflow combined HTTP requests, data transformation, and an AI enrichment step routing through a multi-provider gateway (configured with &lt;code&gt;baseURL: "https://b-lost.com/v1"&lt;/code&gt; for fallback resilience). We monitored server-side metrics via Node.js native &lt;code&gt;process.memoryUsage()&lt;/code&gt; logged every 10 seconds.&lt;/p&gt;

